+## Duel control-window behavior
+
+- Warlock Fear is `SetupThenBreak`: recall the pet, move to preferred casting
+  range, use an available recovery, Life Tap when mana is below 35% and health
+  is above 70%, then permit a direct hard cast to restart pressure. Auto attack,
+  instant damage, channels and area damage stay blocked.
+- Mage Polymorph is `Preserve`: use non-damaging utility and begin Frostbolt
+  only when cast plus projectile travel is expected to land at least 100 ms
+  after Polymorph expires.
+- Hunter Freezing Trap and Shaman Hex are `Preserve`; short Scatter-style
+  setup can become `SetupThenBreak` when it is not part of the trap plan.
+- Rogue Sap/long Blind is `Reset`; a short Gouge-style disorient is setup.
+- Priest fear repositions before pressure. Cyclone is damage immune and only
+  permits an expiry-timed precast, never an early intentional break.
+- Repeat Fear/Polymorph with an existing periodic damage aura. The expected
+  control window must shrink to 1.2 seconds so the bot does not plan a long
+  recovery against a control that the next DoT tick may end.
+- Follow or formation movement owned outside PvP Tactical must not stall
+  recovery, resource preparation or other control-window utility.
+- In arena/battleground contexts, the same breakable control stays `Preserve`
+  until ArenaTeamPlan explicitly owns the CC purpose; no solo release applies.
